    Pass in the answer, like we passed in today
    
    The tests couldn't choose what the bank says: buyCoffee() makes its own
    BankCardReader, and the bank approves or declines at random. It's the
    same problem as printStatus() reading the clock, so this tries the same
    fix. buyCoffee() is handed the answer instead of asking for it.
    
    The tests now pass every run. But look at what moved: buyCoffee() no
    longer charges anything. Charging 450 cents is now main's job, and every
    caller has to remember to do it, with the right amount, before calling
    buyCoffee(). That part is exactly as untestable as before; it just
    isn't in buyCoffee() any more.
    
    We wanted to control the bank's answer without taking away the charge.

